   "subject": "Annotate tree with extra data by node",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"1\">Hey!</font></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"1\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"1\">I&#39;ve been playing around with ggtree -- thanks for the superb package.</font></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"1\"><br></font></span></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.2px\">I&#39;m trying to plot a tree with additional data, like the great set up you have with the dot plot/bar chart to the side of it. But instead of having a data point for every tip label, is it possible to have a data point for node id&#39;s i.e. if I want to plot median patristic distance within a </span></font><span style=\"font-size:19.2px\">monophyletic</span><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.2px\"> group, I could have a dot plot next to the tree showing the median distance in each </span></font></font><font color=\"#000000\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:x-small\">monophyletic</font><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:x-small\"><span style=\"font-size:19.2px\"> phylogroup? I tried playing around, but couldn&#39;t figure it out!</span></font></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"1\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"1\">So basically, use the node id&#39;s instead of tr$tip.label here.</font></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-stretch:normal;font-size:1rem;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;color:rgb(86,116,130);word-wrap:normal;background-color:rgb(243,246,250);border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(220,230,240);border-radius:0.3rem;line-height:1.45;overflow:auto\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;background:transparent;border-radius:0.3rem;font-size:1rem;word-break:normal;display:inline;line-height:inherit;word-wrap:normal\">tr &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(24,54,145)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">rtree</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,134,179)\">30</span>)\r\n\r\nd1 &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(24,54,145)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">data.frame</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">id=</span>tr$tip.label, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">val=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">rnorm</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,134,179)\">30</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">sd=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,134,179)\">3</span>))\r\np &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(24,54,145)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">ggtree</span>(tr)\r\n\r\np2 &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(24,54,145)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">facet_plot</span>(p, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">panel=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(24,54,145)\">&quot;dot&quot;</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">data=</span>d1, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">geom=</span>geom_point, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">aes</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">x=</span>val), <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">color=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(24,54,145)\">&#39;firebrick&#39;</span>)\r\nd2 &lt;-<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(24,54,145)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">data.frame</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">id=</span>tr$tip.label, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">value =</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">abs</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93)\">rnorm</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,134,179)\">30</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">mean=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,134,179)\">100</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(121,93,163)\">sd=</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,134,179)\">50</span>)))</code></pre></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"1\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"1\">Rad package,</font></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"1\">Edyth</font></span></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
