   "date": "2017-06-19T03:32:52Z",
   "subject": "Re: Annotate tree with extra data by node",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Currently <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">facet_plot</code> only work for tips.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I  think it is not a good idea to support aligning data on the right hand  side for internal nodes as it is hard to associate the data to internal  nodes for us using human eye.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">You can use <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">geom_nodepoint</code> to add data point on nodes and encode you data value as point size or color.</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PHAgc3R5bGU9Im1hcmdpbjogMHB4IDBweCAxLjJlbTsiPkN1cnJlbnRseSBgZmFjZXRfcGxvdGAg\r\nb25seSB3b3JrIGZvciB0aXBzLjwvcD48cCBzdHlsZT0ibWFyZ2luOiAwcHggMHB4IDEuMmVtOyI+\r\nSQogdGhpbmsgaXQgaXMgbm90IGEgZ29vZCBpZGVhIHRvIHN1cHBvcnQgYWxpZ25pbmcgZGF0YSBv\r\nbiB0aGUgcmlnaHQgaGFuZCAKc2lkZSBmb3IgaW50ZXJuYWwgbm9kZXMgYXMgaXQgaXMgaGFyZCB0\r\nbyBhc3NvY2lhdGUgdGhlIGRhdGEgdG8gaW50ZXJuYWwgCm5vZGVzIGZvciB1cyB1c2luZyBodW1h\r\nbiBleWUuPC9wPjxwIHN0eWxlPSJtYXJnaW46IDBweCAwcHggMS4yZW07Ij48YnI+PC9wPllvdSBj\r\nYW4gdXNlIGBnZW9tX25vZGVwb2ludGAgdG8gYWRkIGRhdGEgcG9pbnQgb24gbm9kZXMgYW5kIGVu\r\nY29kZSB5b3UgZGF0YSB2YWx1ZSBhcyBwb2ludCBzaXplIG9yIGNvbG9yLjxicj48YnI+PGJyPg==\" style=\"min-height:0;width:0;max-height:0;max-width:0;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0;margin:0\">​</div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Jun 14, 2017 at 5:27 PM, Edyth Parker <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">edyth2...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"1\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Hey!</font></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"1\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"1\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">I&#39;ve been playing around with ggtree -- thanks for the superb package.</font></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:19.2px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"1\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.2px\">I&#39;m trying to plot a tree with additional data, like the great set up you have with the dot plot/bar chart to the side of it. But instead of having a data point for every tip label, is it possible to have a data point for node id&#39;s i.e. if I want to plot median patristic distance within a </span></font><span style=\"font-size:19.2px\">monophyletic</span><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.2px\"> group, I could have a dot plot next to the tree showing the median distance in each </span></font></font><font style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:x-small\" color=\"#000000\">monophyletic</font><font style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:x-small\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:19.2px\"> phylogroup? I tried playing around, but couldn&#39;t figure it out!</span></font></div><div style=\"font-family:a